  "interpretation": "Changing the load-balance weight from zero through 0.1 did not produce an OOD or worst-environment improvement. Zero balance reduced routing entropy to 0.814 while retaining all eight experts, but its randomized-route dependence fell to 0.00061 and accuracy declined. This separates nonuniform expert use from useful adaptive routing: sharper specialization alone is not sufficient.",
